  "reasoning": "The defendants were the actual controller and legal representative of a coal mine. Their negligence and failure to enforce safety measures led to a roof collapse that killed four workers. They also concealed the accident. Under Chinese criminal law, persons in charge of production safety who, through negligence, cause a major accident resulting in death are liable for the crime of ‘重大责任事故罪’. The concealment is encompassed in this offense. No other distinct offenses (e.g., failure to report) are typically charged separately in such cases, so the appropriate charge is the major responsibility accident crime.",
  "final_answer": "[罪名]重大责任事故<eoa>"
}
